# SPA fallback. This file is REQUIRED, not an optimisation.
#
# Routing is client-side (react-router), so only `/index.html` exists on disk.
# Without this rule every area page — /breakdown-recovery-bolton and the other
# 34 in sitemap.xml — returns a hard 404 when opened directly or refreshed,
# including to Googlebot. That would sink the entire per-area SEO strategy the
# site is built around.
#
# The 200 (rather than 301/302) is what makes it a rewrite: the URL stays put
# and React renders the right region. Real files on disk (sitemap.xml,
# robots.txt, /assets/*) are served before this rule is consulted.
#
# Understood by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.

/*    /index.html   200
